Z||000002||DRH||02-08-2000||03:51 PM||||William,<P>Be aware that with no belt the motor heats VERY quickly. I doubt you could make it more than a mile ot two. Even then you could be creating some dangerous hot spots in the motor.<P>David.||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||02-08-2000||05:27 PM||||Monkey,<P>Yes!  The VP came down from the frigid North and over rode my bosses opinion that I could put it in the building.  From what I understand the VP was very HOT about it being in there too.  <P>DRH,<P>Don't get me wrong, I have a belt on the vehicle.  It is not tensioned properly though.  The belt does provide enough tension to replenish the charge in the battery but not with all accessories on and therefore I am making the assumption that it is providing adequate cooling to the engine as well.  I also let the car idle for near 45 minutes with this loose belt to determine if the car was/is driveable.  Temperatures seemed to be normal.<P>William T. Thorn, III<p>[This message has been edited by william_thorniii (edited 02-08-2000).]||||reg||5
