Z||000008||william_thorniii||02-09-2000||05:38 PM||||Bengal, 2m4 & 56,<P>Thanks guys!  I really appreciate the offers.  My car has been sitting since the week after Thanksgiving.  I drove it the other night about 500 yards and remembered how much I loved it.  After all it is the Fiero that started it all for me.  I can't wait much longer until she is back on the road.  <P>Bill,<P>Although I truly appreciate your offer, I would prefer to complete the necessary repairs closer to where the car is presently located.  Thereby helping to ensure that I don't suffer more damage in transit.  If either of the others don't pan out, I will definitely look you up.   <P>Scott & Drew,<P>My work schedule pretty much guarantees that I will need to do this on the weekend.  If the weather holds a driveway would be heaven (OOPS, didn't mean to reference that religion thread from the O/T section!).  In fact I had never worked in an enclosed area until last Wednesday.  Even if it turns cold a driveway is much better than the still snow covered and rather puddled parking lot in which the vehicle sits presently.  <P>Guys, in order to inconvenience you as little as possible, what are your schedules this weekend?  Ideally it should not take me terribly long.  All that I should need is some running water to refill the radiator system and perhaps another pair of hands for a minute while re-installing the belt. <P>Let me know, I am keeping my calendar open.<P>William T. Thorn, III <BR>937-259-5295||||reg||14
